<Project>

  <!--
    Imported by every package that ships types. The meta-package does not import it: it holds no code, so
    there is no surface to baseline.

    The public surface is the product here: these libraries ship types and nothing else. The analyzer holds
    it to a committed baseline, so every change to it is a reviewed diff — an undeclared public symbol
    raises RS0016, and a declared symbol that no longer exists raises RS0017. Both are warnings locally and
    errors in CI, where the warning ratchet promotes them. Decision: ADR-0018.

    Build-time only: PrivateAssets keeps the analyzer out of any package this project produces.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.PublicApiAnalyzers" Version="3.3.4" PrivateAssets="all" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    ONE baseline per project, shared by all six target frameworks rather than one per framework. The
    attributes do not vary by target — the surface is the same everywhere — so a single file states that
    intent and makes a divergence between two targets a failure rather than something each baseline would
    quietly absorb. The condition guards the outer, framework-less evaluation of a multi-targeting project.

    Since ADR-0027 each catalogue is its own package, so each carries its own baseline: a change to one
    work's surface can no longer hide in another's diff.
  -->
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' != ''">
    <AdditionalFiles Include="$(MSBuildProjectDirectory)\PublicAPI\PublicAPI.Shipped.txt" />
    <AdditionalFiles Include="$(MSBuildProjectDirectory)\PublicAPI\PublicAPI.Unshipped.txt" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
